config BACKPORTS_DEBUG
	bool "Enable backports debugging"
	depends on BACKPORTS
	help
	  Enable debugging features for backports components.
	  This adds additional logging and diagnostic capabilities
	  to help troubleshoot backports-related issues.

	  This option increases kernel size and may impact performance.
	  Only enable for development and debugging purposes.

config BACKPORTS_DEBUG_VERBOSE
	bool "Enable verbose debugging output"
	depends on BACKPORTS_DEBUG
	help
	  Enable verbose debugging output for backports components.
	  This provides detailed logging of internal operations,
	  function calls, and data structures.

	  WARNING: This generates significant log output and can
	  impact system performance. Only enable for detailed
	  debugging and development work.

	  Verbose debugging includes:
	  - Function entry/exit logging
	  - Parameter and return value logging
	  - Internal state transitions
	  - Detailed error reporting

	  Say Y only if you need detailed debugging information.

