config BACKPORTS_TRACING
	bool "Enable backports tracing support"
	depends on BACKPORTS && TRACING
	help
	  Enable tracing support for backports components using
	  the kernel's tracing infrastructure. This provides
	  low-overhead tracing of backports operations.

	  Tracing features include:
	  - Function tracing with minimal overhead
	  - Event tracing for key operations
	  - Performance profiling support
	  - Integration with ftrace and perf

	  This is useful for:
	  - Performance analysis
	  - Debugging timing issues
	  - Understanding code flow
	  - Profiling backports operations

	  Requires CONFIG_TRACING to be enabled.

	  Say Y to enable backports tracing support.

config BACKPORTS_STATISTICS
	bool "Enable backports statistics collection"
	depends on BACKPORTS
	help
	  Enable collection of detailed statistics for backports
	  components. This provides runtime statistics about
	  operations, performance, and resource usage.

	  Statistics include:
	  - Frame transmission and reception counts
	  - Error rates and retry statistics
	  - Performance metrics and timing
	  - Resource usage information

	  Statistics are available through:
	  - /proc/net/backports/ interface
	  - debugfs entries (if enabled)
	  - sysfs attributes

	  This is useful for:
	  - Performance monitoring
	  - Troubleshooting issues
	  - System optimization
	  - Usage analysis

	  Say Y to enable statistics collection.

