	  wireless drivers without requiring kernel recompilation.

	  Runtime switching features:
	  - Dynamic driver loading/unloading
	  - Configuration preservation during switches
	  - Interface state management
	  - Seamless transition support
	  - User-space control interface

	  This allows users to switch between backports and vendor
	  drivers at runtime for testing and comparison purposes.

	  WARNING: Runtime switching may cause temporary network
	  disruption and should be used carefully.

	  Say Y to enable runtime driver switching.

