# Kernel Version Compatibility Layer
#

config BACKPORTS_KERNEL_COMPAT
	bool "Enable kernel version compatibility layer"
	default y
	depends on BACKPORTS
	help
	  Enable kernel version compatibility layer that provides
	  compatibility shims and API adaptations for different
	  kernel versions.

	  The compatibility layer provides:
	  - Kernel API compatibility shims
	  - Android kernel 4.19 specific optimizations
	  - Mobile platform power management integration
	  - Regulatory compliance enforcement
	  - Cross-version wireless stack compatibility

	  This is essential for supporting wireless drivers across
	  different kernel versions and platforms.

	  Say Y to enable kernel compatibility layer.

config BACKPORTS_ANDROID_COMPAT
	bool "Enable Android kernel compatibility"
	default y if ANDROID
	depends on BACKPORTS_KERNEL_COMPAT
	help
	  Enable Android-specific compatibility features including
	  integration with Android's power management, security
	  model, and wireless framework.

	  Android compatibility includes:
	  - Android wakelock integration
	  - Android power management optimization
	  - Android security policy compliance
	  - Android property system integration
	  - Android framework callbacks

	  This is required for proper operation on Android kernels.

	  Say Y if building for Android kernel.

config BACKPORTS_MOBILE_PLATFORM_COMPAT
	bool "Enable mobile platform optimizations"
	default y if ARM || ARM64 || ANDROID
	depends on BACKPORTS_KERNEL_COMPAT
	help
	  Enable mobile platform specific optimizations including
	  power management, battery optimization, and performance
	  tuning for ARM-based mobile devices.

	  Mobile platform optimizations include:
	  - Advanced power management
	  - Battery optimization algorithms
	  - Mobile-specific memory management
	  - Suspend/resume optimization
	  - Runtime power management integration

	  This is recommended for ARM-based mobile devices.

	  Say Y for mobile platforms.

config BACKPORTS_REGULATORY_ENFORCEMENT
	bool "Enable regulatory compliance enforcement"
	default y
	depends on BACKPORTS_KERNEL_COMPAT
	help
	  Enable strict regulatory compliance enforcement across
	  different kernel versions and regulatory domains.

	  Regulatory enforcement includes:
	  - Cross-version regulatory API compatibility
	  - Domain-specific feature restrictions
	  - Monitor mode and injection compliance
	  - Power limit enforcement
	  - Channel restriction enforcement

	  This ensures compliance with local regulations.

	  Say Y to enable regulatory enforcement.

config BACKPORTS_POWER_COMPAT
	bool "Enable power management compatibility"
	default y if BACKPORTS_MOBILE_PLATFORM_COMPAT
	depends on BACKPORTS_KERNEL_COMPAT
	help
	  Enable power management compatibility layer for mobile
	  platforms with battery optimization and suspend/resume
	  support.

	  Power management compatibility includes:
	  - Runtime power management integration
	  - Battery optimization algorithms
	  - Suspend/resume state management
	  - Mobile platform power hints
	  - Android power management integration

	  This is essential for proper power management on mobile
	  devices and Android platforms.

	  Say Y to enable power management compatibility.

# End of kernel compatibility configuration